{"ts":"2026-08-08T06:28:19.610Z","type":"attempt","frontier":"operation-progress-store-persistence-main","rung":"observe","rungIndex":1,"prevRungIndex":0,"hypothesis":"Real persistence for the rebalancer's DurableWorkflowCoordinator (audit findings 15+18; explicit-choice recorded = WIRE REAL PERSISTENCE, preferred — a projection rename would have abandoned the transition-history witness restart-recovery and fence decisions genuinely need). New operation-workflow-persistence.js: persistOperationWorkflowTransitionToDurableRow is a FAIL-CLOSED persist callback (no longer the no-op) following the four-subsystem template (managed-merge/split, control-plane readiness, schema-provisioning) — it accepts only candidates whose transition history strictly appends onto the durable basis (durableBasisStepCount stamped from the row's steps_history at recovery) and throws DURABLE_ROW_NOT_EXTENDED otherwise so the coordinator rolls memory back; recoverOperationWorkflowsFromDurableRows + buildOperationWorkflowRowLoader hydrate the witness via coordinator.recover; isOperationWorkflowTerminalForPersistence closes terminal records. rebalance-coordinator-lifecycle.js constructs the default coordinator with the real callback + terminal predicate; operation-workflow-owner-execution-lane.js ensureOperationWorkflow recovers from the durable row BEFORE creating an empty record (witness survives restart). Lease/fence freshness no longer hardcoded CURRENT (new operation-workflow-port-freshness.js wired into operation-workflow-owner-ports.js): lease freshness derives from the Q9 durable row lease (ACTIVE->CURRENT, EXPIRED->STALE, legacy->UNAVAILABLE via resolveOperationOwnerLeaseState); the publication fence compares the persisted witness against the row's steps_history mirror over the durable basis with typed CURRENT/STALE/INCOMPLETE (never raw null), hydrating on first observation after restart. Red-on-revert verified three ways (persist->no-op, lease->CURRENT, fence->CURRENT each flip assertions red); 24-assertion suite; 2/2 receipts; full rebalancer corpus 206/206 (8229 assertions) + test/node 55/55; independent verifier APPROVED (evidence subagent:ses_01ff3071effen423SGKJ1lhfTK).","changeRef":"diff:solve/changes/operation-progress-store-persistence/attempt-1.diff.json","metricBefore":null,"metricAfter":0,"metricDirection":"lower-is-better","invalidSample":false,"baselineAbsent":true,"done":true,"evidence":"solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","beforeEvidence":"solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","beforeEvidenceIdentity":{"path":"solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","resolvedPath":"/media/peter/4509da27-4751-4dee-b366-f3983d0777252/peter/projects/lagrange/solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","exists":false,"size":null,"mtimeMs":null,"sha256":null,"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["progress-store-durable-or-honestly-renamed","lease-fence-freshness-not-hardcoded"]},"observedAt":"2026-08-07T14:20:46.688Z","fingerprint":"4b0bccd3f90b587d8834fad6637c2d39a1173debb048f5a1560b895a3b9ace58"},"beforeEvidenceFingerprint":"4b0bccd3f90b587d8834fad6637c2d39a1173debb048f5a1560b895a3b9ace58","evidenceIdentity":{"path":"solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","resolvedPath":"/media/peter/4509da27-4751-4dee-b366-f3983d0777252/peter/projects/lagrange/solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","exists":true,"size":2400,"mtimeMs":1786170381164.6243,"sha256":"c7cbabefbe3d34751591e7034e2d09d663d40ac10938a1fd0d03050e0c9554aa","probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/operation-progress-store-persistence.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["progress-store-durable-or-honestly-renamed","lease-fence-freshness-not-hardcoded"]},"observedAt":"2026-08-08T06:28:19.589Z","fingerprint":"e929ff2f1b86fa79da4759050ebbf2f51d583